      "writtenOn": "2025-01-21T17:27:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The chosen approach is not acceptable in my opinion because it may lead to incorrect alignment of the spinlocks. I don\u0027t see what guarantees that __alignof__(struct sbitmap_word) is a multiple of __alignof__(spinlock_t)? Even if that requirement would be met today, any future change in either data structure could break the alignment assumption. I think that it would be much cleaner to move the `struct sbitmap_word` definition into a private header file and to add a spinlock_t member in that data structure.",
      "parentUuid": "ec7e38e9_5635508f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 145,
        "startChar": 38,
        "endLine": 145,
        "endChar": 77
      },
      "revId": "05b2adb1d4c5b655103af327d56c280ba4c8d847",
